export anchor LuxuryStyle:
    number: 17
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Luxury
    idea: An ivory house style with thin, widely tracked capitals, a dark gold accent, hairline rules and a great deal of quiet space.
    base: light
    palette:
        ivory: #faf7f0, the page
        stone: #f3eee3, the style sheet ground
        ink: #1e1b16, text and the primary button
        taupe: #5e574b, capital labels and last week's dashed line
        darkGold: #7a5c1e, the accent, progress fills, this week's line, the focus outline and At risk
        hairline: #d9d0bd, rules between entries and sections and progress tracks
        sage: #3d5a40, On track
        oxblood: #8e2f22, Behind and the overdue figure and word
    type:
        Display face Didot, Didot LT STD, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Big Caslon,
        Libre Bodoni, Hoefler Text, Garamond, Times New Roman, serif, always
        regular weight. The wordmark is 40px capitals with 0.42em tracking,
        the greeting 56px italic, summary figures 72px, section titles 22px
        capitals with 0.36em tracking and project names 24px capitals with
        0.16em tracking. Body is Avenir Next, Avenir, Gill Sans, Helvetica
        Neue, Segoe UI, system-ui, sans-serif at 15px regular and 1.7 line
        height. Labels are 11px sans capitals with 0.28em tracking in taupe.
    layout:
        One centred column 880px wide. A slim utility row shows the date on
        the left and an underlined search, Notices · 3 and Mara Okafor on
        the right, over a hairline. A centred masthead holds the spaced
        wordmark, a 40px gold rule and a centred row of spaced capital nav
        links with a gold underline on Home. The greeting is centred with
        much space around it, a capital date line, the italic greeting, one
        sentence about the four overdue tasks and two buttons. Each later
        section opens with a hairline and a centred spaced title over a
        small caption, The Week as a two by two grid of large figures split
        by hairlines, The Portfolio as one project per row with an italic
        gold No. 1, the name, the percent, a capital meta line, the status
        and a hairline progress track, The Fortnight as a thin line chart
        over a two row table of daily values, and Correspondence as rows of
        time beside a name and a sentence. Below 720px the wordmark
        shrinks, rows stack and the figure grid stays two by two.
    spacing: An 8px unit used generously. 96px between sections, 36px inside portfolio rows and 40px inside figure cells.
    density: Very sparse. One or two elements per row.
    corners: Square throughout. Only the palette swatches are round.
    borders: 1px hairline rules in #d9d0bd between entries and sections, a 1px ink rule above the style sheet and a 40px gold rule under the wordmark. Progress fills are a 3px gold line on the hairline track.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        No pictograms. Status is a 12px thin outline mark beside a tracked
        capital word, a circle for On track in sage, a lozenge for At risk
        in gold and a struck square for Behind in oxblood. Notifications
        are the word Notices with a count. The chart uses hollow taupe dots
        on a dashed line for last week and solid gold dots on a solid line
        for this week.
    focus: A 2px dark gold outline offset 4px. A focused field gets a 2px gold underline as well.
    tone: Courteous and composed, with titled sections such as The Week, The Portfolio, The Fortnight and Correspondence, and small numbers written as words in prose.
